{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function asyncRetry<TFn>(fn, initialOptions?): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/async-retryer.ts#L667","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-retryer.ts:667"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a retry-enabled version of an async function. This is a convenience wrapper\naround the AsyncRetryer class that returns the execute method."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AnyAsyncFunction.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The async function to add retry functionality to"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AsyncRetryerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AsyncRetryerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration options for the retry behavior"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new function that executes the original with retry logic"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Awaited"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReturnType"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">> | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Define your async function normally\nasync function fetchData(url: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(url)\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Request failed')\n  return response.json()\n}\n\n// Create retry-enabled function\nconst fetchWithRetry = asyncRetry(fetchData, {\n  maxAttempts: 3,\n  backoff: 'exponential',\n  baseWait: 1000,\n  jitter: 0.1\n})\n\n// Call it multiple times\nconst data1 = await fetchWithRetry('/api/data1')\nconst data2 = await fetchWithRetry('/api/data2')","lang":"typescript"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"initialoptions","text":"initialOptions?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction asyncRetry<TFn>(fn, initialOptions?): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-retryer.ts:667](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/async-retryer.ts#L667)\n\nCreates a retry-enabled version of an async function. This is a convenience wrapper\naround the AsyncRetryer class that returns the execute method.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* [`AnyAsyncFunction`](../type-aliases/AnyAsyncFunction.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\nThe async function to add retry functionality to\n\n### initialOptions?\n\n[`AsyncRetryerOptions`](../interfaces/AsyncRetryerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`\\> = `{}`\n\nConfiguration options for the retry behavior\n\n## Returns\n\nA new function that executes the original with retry logic\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```typescript\n// Define your async function normally\nasync function fetchData(url: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(url)\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Request failed')\n  return response.json()\n}\n\n// Create retry-enabled function\nconst fetchWithRetry = asyncRetry(fetchData, {\n  maxAttempts: 3,\n  backoff: 'exponential',\n  baseWait: 1000,\n  jitter: 0.1\n})\n\n// Call it multiple times\nconst data1 = await fetchWithRetry('/api/data1')\nconst data2 = await fetchWithRetry('/api/data2')\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: asyncRetry\ntitle: asyncRetry\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction asyncRetry<TFn>(fn, initialOptions?): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-retryer.ts:667](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/pacer/src/async-retryer.ts#L667)\n\nCreates a retry-enabled version of an async function. This is a convenience wrapper\naround the AsyncRetryer class that returns the execute method.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* [`AnyAsyncFunction`](../type-aliases/AnyAsyncFunction.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\nThe async function to add retry functionality to\n\n### initialOptions?\n\n[`AsyncRetryerOptions`](../interfaces/AsyncRetryerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`\\> = `{}`\n\nConfiguration options for the retry behavior\n\n## Returns\n\nA new function that executes the original with retry logic\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```typescript\n// Define your async function normally\nasync function fetchData(url: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(url)\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Request failed')\n  return response.json()\n}\n\n// Create retry-enabled function\nconst fetchWithRetry = asyncRetry(fetchData, {\n  maxAttempts: 3,\n  backoff: 'exponential',\n  baseWait: 1000,\n  jitter: 0.1\n})\n\n// Call it multiple times\nconst data1 = await fetchWithRetry('/api/data1')\nconst data2 = await fetchWithRetry('/api/data2')\n```\n"}
